    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote 51 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. Each client keeps a queue of `(time, cost)` records, oldest first, and expired records are dropped on each call when they are at least `window_seconds` old. `allow` only records accepted requests, and `remaining` and `retry_after` record nothing. `retry_after` walks the live records in order and returns the wait until enough units have expired for the cost to fit. The limiter tracks the largest `now` seen across all methods and raises `ValueError` on any earlier time. Validation rejects `bool` and non-integer limits and costs, non-positive or NaN windows, and non-numeric or NaN times. I did not measure line coverage, since the coverage tool was not part of the run. The one line not exercised is the unreachable fallback at the end of `retry_after`, which carries a `# pragma: no cover` comment that the gate will ignore. Coverage should still be above 90%, but that is an estimate.",
